                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SimpSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            for short, is the category whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+maps"} simplicial maps
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"}> Equivalently
            , this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SimpSet
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SimpSet \simeq [\Delta^{op}, Set]
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p
            Many basic properties of the category of simplicial sets follow as it being a special case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            (namely over the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
          %p
            For example, this immediately implies (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves#GeneralProperties"} here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            constructed levelwise) and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
          %p In this vein:
          %p
          #EpimorphismsOfSimplicialSetsDetectedDegreewise.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \xrightarrow{f_\bullet} Y_\bullet
              of simplicial sets is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  precisely if all component
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  precisely if all component
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This is the immediate specialization of
              %a{:href => "category+of+presheaves#EpimorphismsOfPresheavesAreDetectedObjectwise"} this Proposition
              for general presheaves.
          %h3#cartesian_closed_monoidal_structure Cartesian closed monoidal structure
          %p
            As described at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
            the cartesian tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes T = S \times T
            of simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the simplicial set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (S \otimes T) : [n] \mapsto S_n \times T_n
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the product on the right is the cartesian product in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            One central reason why simplicial sets are useful and important is that this simple monoidal structure (“disturbingly simple minded” in the words of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0809/0809.4221v1.pdf#page=24"} Friedman08, p. 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\cdot| : SSet \to Top
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              simplicial sets, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    |S \times T| \simeq |S| \times |T|
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right the cartesian product is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} nice category
              of compactly generated Hausdorff spaces.
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products+of+simplices"} products of simplices
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            As described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S,T]
            of simplicial sets is the simplicial set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [S,T] : [n] \mapsto Hom_{SSet}(S \times \Delta[n], T)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n] = Hom_{\mathbf{\Delta}}(-,[n])
            is the standard simplicial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \in \mathbf{\Delta}
            under the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          %h3#adjunctions Adjunctions
          %p
            The maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N: \Cat \rightarrow \Simp\Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Top
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S: \Top \rightarrow \Simp\Set
            described in the examples are actually functors, both of which have left adjoints. These adjoint pairs are examples of a very general sort of adjunction involving simplicial sets, of which there are many examples.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be any cocomplete category and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \Delta \rightarrow E
            be a functor. We define the right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : E \rightarrow \Simp\Set
            as follows. Given an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
            the
            = succeed "-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Re
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Re
            are defined to be the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(F[n],e)
            of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[n]
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is defined on morphisms by postcomposition.
          %p
            The left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is defined to be the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            along the Yoneda embedding
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y: \Delta \rightarrow \Simp\Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            is full and faithful, we will have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ly
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ly = F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L (\Delta[n]) = F[n]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            on the represented simplicial sets;
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is the unique cocontinuous extension of this functor to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Simp\Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted colimit
          %p
            (Easy)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} abstract nonsense
            shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjoint pair
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
          %p Here are some examples:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \Cat
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                be the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \mapsto [n]
                (the inclusion of posets into categories). The right adjoint is the nerve functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                described above. The left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\tau}_1
                takes a simplicial set to its
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong fundamental category
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \Top
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                be the functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↦
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \mapsto {\Delta}_n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                described above. The left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-|
                is called
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                is the standard
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Delta}^n
            %li
              %p
                (Barycentric) subdivision and extension
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} sd
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                        %mo ↔
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sd: \Simp\Set \leftrightarrow \Simp\Set :\ex
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
                functor and its left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                      %mo ↔
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Simp\Set \leftrightarrow \Simp\Cat
                where
                %span.newWikiWord
                  SimpCat
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/SimpCat"} ?
                denotes the category of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Simp\Set
            %li
              %p
                The adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                      %mo ↔
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \times X: \SimpSet \leftrightarrow \SimpSet :(-)^X
                between the product with a simplicial set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and the internal-hom, which makes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Simp
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Simp\Set
                into a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
                equipped with an “interval”
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered object
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
                equipped with distinct top and bottom elements. Then we have the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \to E
                sending
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
                to the subobject
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi …
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ (x_1,x_2,\dots,x_n) \;|\; x_1 \le x_2 \le \dots \le x_n \} \hookrightarrow I^n
                which gives rise to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to \SimpSet
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \SimpSet
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
                of such “intervals”.
          %h3#model_category_structures Model category structures
          %p
            There are important
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoids
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                presents the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
          %h3#internal_logic Internal logic
          %p
            Like any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \SimpSet
            has an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                It is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+topos"} two-valued topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \Delta^0
                are
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %li
              %p
                It is not
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
                of a simplicial subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq B
                is the
                %em full
                simplicial subset on the vertices of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                not contained in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                (“full” meaning it contains a simplex of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                as soon as it contains all its vertices). Thus,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\cup \neg A = B
                only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                lies entirely in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                By
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SimpSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \SimpSet
                therefore does not satisfy the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %li
              %p
                Like any presheaf topos, it satisfies
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+choice"} dependent choice
                (assuming it holds in the metatheory); see
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#FourmanScedrov"} Fourman and Scedrov
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
                is simply the discrete simplicial set of ordinary natural numbers.
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, it satisfies
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov%27s+principle"} Markov's principle
            %li
              %p
                Less obviously, it satisfies the
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Kreisel-Putnam axiom
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Kreisel-Putnam+axiom"} ?
                that
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\neg p \to (q\vee r)) = ((\neg p \to q) \vee (\neg p \to r))
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/159989/internal-logic-of-the-topos-of-simplicial-sets/"} this MO question
                and answers.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asSet"} asSet
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                = succeed ")" do
